- Extended the `executable_hashes` table to hash Mach-O executable files, not only app bundles. A new `path_type` column reports `bundle` or `file`, `executable_path` resolves symlinks for files, and files that are not Mach-O executables return no row. Hashes are cached per file on inode, size and change time, symlinks and hard links to one file are hashed once, the bytes hashed per query are capped so a large tree is hashed over several runs, and an unreadable file no longer fails the whole query: a Mach-O file that cannot be read returns no row, and an app bundle whose executable cannot be read still returns its row with an empty hash.
